From 95e3d3cf3511161124e5f96a6dd9159373560a56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:29:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Close merged-path fail-opens in the
 no-required-check CI fallback

Follow-up to review t_01a1daca670511da of PR #2830 (both are narrow fail-opens
on the MERGED path of the no-required-check fallback; the required-check path
is unchanged).

1. A completed 0-run check suite that did not pass (workflow failed before
   creating jobs: failure, cancelled, timed_out, action_required,
   startup_failure, stale or no conclusion) was ignored once the PR was MERGED,
   because fallback_outcomes only added empty-suite rows when not merged.
   It is now a `failure` row on both paths. On the merged path a suite
   provably created after mergedAt (e.g. a main-push workflow on the landed
   sha) is post-merge evidence instead; a tied or unreadable creation time
   fails closed (counts as failure). Passing or still-open empty suites keep
   their prior semantics (OPEN missing, MERGED ignored).

2. _unsuperseded (merge_time, distinct_suites path) dropped an earlier failure
   whenever a later same-name run in the same suite started after it ended,
   which cannot tell a rerun from a later sibling job (max-parallel:1 matrix
   with a static job name). A run is now superseded only by a proven rerun:
   both resolve through the Actions jobs API (check_run_url names the check
   run, head_sha matches) to the same workflow run id with a higher
   run_attempt, and every same-key run (pre- and post-merge) resolves to a
   distinct (run id, attempt), i.e. one such job per attempt. Non-Actions apps,
   unreadable jobs (401/403/404) and ambiguous attempts keep the earlier run
   (fail closed). The jobs API is read only when chronology already suggests
   a rerun.

Proof:
- RED: 34 of the 41 new cases in test_kanban_pr_fallback_merged.py fail on
  edee8e41 (the review probes: MERGED + green run + failed empty suite ->
  success; failure ended 12:10, sibling started 12:20 -> success). The other
  7 are controls (passing empty suites, proven rerun chain).
- GREEN: 19 consumer files (every test importing the touched modules)
  515 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped.
- Mutants: 19/19 killed (every new condition, incl. the old chronology-only
  rule and the old OPEN-only empty-suite rule).
